  "headline": "Across all 170 scored prompts with a known outcome, higher prompt scores are associated with fewer turns to done (Spearman -0.239, p=0.003) and, over 229, a higher achieved rate (Spearman 0.234, p=0.001). Rubric split: low-scored prompts (<=4, n=145) took 1.641 turns to done vs 1.333 for high-scored (>=7, n=3): ratio 1.23x, permutation p=0.8152, Cliff's delta 0.062. Achieved rate 0.46 vs 0.667 (p=0.5986); only 3 prompts scored >= 7, so that split is underpowered. Associated with, not caused by. 53 of 665 prompts dropped by the confidentiality filter before grading.",
